WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.591
A new rider starts on Connect Bike. This slice draws it as designed: pair the bike

00:00:07.591 --> 00:00:09.480
once, then take the class.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.840
At rest, the screen has the wordmark, the bike, one button, and the bikes it works

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.830
with. The hint under the button is gone, and nothing else is there.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.183
Press the button, by touch or by keyboard, and the browser opens its list of bikes.

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:32.244
While it is open, the card says it is looking for bikes nearby.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.453
Pick the bike, and the card names it while the button says pairing. When the bike

00:00:40.453 --> 00:00:42.406
answers, the card gets a check.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.289
Half a second later, the class opens with the bike connected, and the bike is

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:54.196
remembered.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.250
On a phone the photo follows the content. From a wide tablet up, it sits on the

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:04.859
left.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:14.365
Ten new specs were written first, and three failed on the old screen. Now one

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:17.887
hundred and sixty-two specs and every unit test pass.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:28.244
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:29.440
nothing else.

00:01:29.785 --> 00:01:34.737
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:39.749
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:39.749 --> 00:01:43.250
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:43.595 --> 00:01:47.571
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
